{"availability":"available","full":"c0de128/grass-pass","name":"grass-pass","description":"Grass Pass: your ticket to get outside. Printable park treasure-hunt passes built from real park data with open-weight Gemma 4. Hacktoberfest 2026 Week 1.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-05T22:27:06Z","updated":"2026-10-11T04:30:58Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://grass-pass.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://grass-pass.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T05:14:35.473Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T05:14:35.473Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T05:14:35.473Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T06:14:35.518Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T05:14:35.473Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Grass Pass: Family time is back! Powered by AI.","Your ticket to get outside. Pick a park. Print a pass. Phone away.","Try it live: (live since Oct 8, 2026). The example passes open with no sign-in. Your first new pass each day needs no sign-in either; for more, press Try as a judge (one click, no sign-up) or sign in with GitHub or Google."],"features":["Park Finds: what is mapped inside the park on OpenStreetMap (courts, playgrounds, shelters, bridges, ponds...).","Wild Finds: species people photographed within 1.5 km in the last 14 days (iNaturalist, research grade only).","Find This Spot: a black-and-white map of the park's paths with an X on one real landmark, drawn by code, and a","Lucky Finds: \"maybe\" finds (a dog, a bike), only when at least 3 Google reviews of that park from the last 2","October special: real monarch counts near the park, next to the same days last year (all code)."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/c0de128/grass-pass/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9154d60a764d7c03025aa1193f15dd20b1f6222a69994ee2ed92d22c8ff60e40","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:35.657Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14